PicoRV32, upstream https://github.com/YosysHQ/picorv32
Commit ef203c2b0a3fb793280f5114941416c425c5b461 (ISC; see COPYING).
The board instantiates only picorv32.
Configuration: RV32EC, single-port register file, no counters, IRQ, PCPI, MUL
or DIV. Shifts advance one bit per cycle. Firmware uses aligned memory accesses;
misalignment and illegal-instruction traps remain enabled.

Local logic changes:
- PROGADDR_WIDTH (default 32) sizes PC state and branch-target arithmetic;
  the board uses 12 bits for its 4 KiB resident program address space.
- STACKADDR_WIDTH (default 32) sizes x2; the board uses 13 bits to include
  reset SP=4096. All other writable registers, data and MMIO remain 32 bits.
  In particular, ra remains full width because LLVM uses it as a temporary.
- FIXED_GP (default disabled) supplies the board's linker constant 2032 and
  fixes tp at zero. ZERO_REGS additionally removes t1/t2; the firmware build
  reserves these registers and checks disassembly. This is a specialized
  resident firmware ABI, identified by its LRV2 image header.
- Single-port reads share selection decoding and OR mutually exclusive
  register values. Writes are decoded individually, allowing constant and
  narrow registers to disappear without added read muxes.
- Add, subtract and signed/unsigned ordered comparisons share one carry
  chain. Equality retains a parallel comparison.
- AND/OR/XOR share factored Boolean terms and one result selector. Logical
  and arithmetic shifts share the right-shift path.
- ALU results and branch targets share the existing result register.
- Store data comes directly from the held operand and lane-replication logic,
  avoiding a second 32-bit holding register. Stall tests cover all store sizes.

No RAM, DSP or synthesis-mapping substitutions are used for the CPU.
The firmware build validates fixed/reserved registers and local SP usage,
checks a conservative call-graph stack bound, and enforces the 4 KiB layout.
